+
+If any row is ✗, add a note explaining what is missing and why.
+
+## Generation manifest extension
+
+`knowledge/.generation-manifest.json` is a local bookkeeping extension, not an OKF concept document. Use JSON with `schema_version: 1` and a `documents` object keyed by bundle-relative file paths. Each entry contains `output_sha256` (exact bytes last written by the generator) and `sources` (repository-relative file path to exact-byte SHA-256 map). Include generated inventory and indexes; for the log, preserve prior entries when writing a new run. Do not put the manifest's own hash inside itself.
+
+Before an update, compare current outputs to recorded output hashes and current in-scope source files to their recorded source hashes. Added and removed files must affect a directory source snapshot. Protect files with no baseline or modified bytes. Record only outputs actually written under the requested workflow, and never reset hashes for protected content. Write the manifest after successful document writes; if interrupted, treat mismatched outputs conservatively on resume. Validation never updates this manifest.
